WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
The refrigeration cycle is the foundation of everything you'll do in this trade.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Lab: connect manifold gauges to a live system and calculate superheat and
subcooling. Connect blue hose to suction port, red to liquid port. Read
pressures, convert to saturation temps using PT chart, measure actual line

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Target Superheat: Manufacturer-specified superheat at current conditions.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Target Subcooling: Manufacturer-specified subcooling, typically 10-15F for TXV
systems.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: This is the single most important diagnostic
skill in HVAC.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Verify airflow BEFORE connecting gauges. And — Let system
run 15+ minutes before readings

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Before you move on — what happens to refrigerant in the evaporator? Don't look
it up. Think about it.

